- How would you handle flaky E2E tests in your pipeline?
- When would you invest in mutation testing vs. traditional coverage?
- How do you determine when a test has too many dependencies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to reason about real-world flakiness in a simple worker, ensuring correctness under retries and duplicates.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent processing
- Message deduplication
- Backoff and retry strategies
- Mocking external services for CI
- End-to-end vs unit tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// idempotent worker sketch
const seen = new Set();
function handle(msg) {
  if (seen.has(msg.id)) return {status:'skipped'};
  seen.add(msg.id);
  // simulate processing
  return {status:'done'};
}
```

